# Fedora Desktop - Multi-monitor setup
# Copy to outputs.conf on this machine

# Outputs are matched by identifier ("make model serial"), not connector name.
# Connector names are handed out by the GPU and shifted when the RTX 2080 went
# in: the left Acer moved DP-3 -> DP-1, so `output DP-1 disable` began switching
# off the left Acer instead of the 1080p TV, and DP-3 stopped existing entirely.
# Identifiers follow the monitor, so they survive GPU swaps and cable moves.
# Refresh after a hardware change with:
#   swaymsg -t get_outputs -r | jq -r '.[] | "\(.make) \(.model) \(.serial)"'

# Display configuration - boot default is the 2s layout (left Acer + main Acer).
# Every display must be named explicitly: any output not listed here gets
# auto-placed by sway at scale 1, which parks the 4K TV to the right of main.
output "LG Electronics LG TV SSCR2 0x01010101" disable
output "Acer Technologies Acer AL2216W L92080554231" pos 0 390 res 1680x1050
output "Acer Technologies XB271HU #ASP2u3xvGwHd" pos 1680 0 mode 2560x1440@60Hz

# The 1080p LG TV is not plugged into the RTX 2080 (HDMI-A-2 is free for it), so
# its identifier is unknown and it cannot be named here yet. Connect it, run the
# command above, then add a `disable` line for it and hand workspaces 3 and 4
# back their preferred output (TV only, no XB fallback).

# Workspace assignments. Sway sends a workspace to the first *active* output
# in its list. If every listed output is off, or the workspace has no
# assignment, it follows the focused output. Do not give 3/4/6 an XB
# fallback: that pins them to the Predator, so Super+3/4/6 can never stay on
# the left Acer.
workspace 1 output "Acer Technologies XB271HU #ASP2u3xvGwHd"
workspace 2 output "Acer Technologies Acer AL2216W L92080554231"
# workspace 3 output "<1080p TV identifier>"   # when TV1080 is known
# workspace 4 output "<1080p TV identifier>"   # when TV1080 is known
workspace 6 output "LG Electronics LG TV SSCR2 0x01010101"
